course: dictionary
lesson: 16008
title: Variant: a slightly different form
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A variant is a slightly different form or version of something. It is the same thing, changed a little. «Colour» and «color» are two spellings of one word: colour is the usual British spelling, and color is its American variant.
explain: «In our board game, we played a variant where each player had only five turns.» The game is still the same game, but one rule has changed. Always ask: what has changed a little, and what has stayed the same?
explain: In science and the news, a variant can be a changed form of a germ. «Scientists found a new variant of the virus and are checking how fast it spreads.» The virus has changed a little, so it is a variant of the old one.
explain: Variant can also be an adjective, a more formal word meaning different from the usual form. «The teacher wrote the sum in a variant form on the board.» The clue is usual: a variant is what is not the usual way.
fact: A variant is a slightly different form or version of something.
fact: «Colour» and «color» are spelling variants of the same word.
fact: In games, a variant changes one rule.
fact: A new variant of a virus is a form whose genes have changed a little.
fact: As an adjective, variant (formal) means different from the usual form.
exercise: «Colour» and «color» are two spellings of one word. What is «color» in this case? | *A variant of colour | A colour that is a kind of animal | A rule of a game | A new virus
exercise: «We played a variant of chess where each piece moved one square less.» What is a variant here? | A game with no pieces | A chess board made of wood | *A version of the game with one rule changed | A prize for the winner
exercise: Which word means a slightly different form of something? | shop | cake | *variant | usual
test: «The doctors studied the new variant of the germ to see how fast it spread.» What is a variant of a germ? | A germ that has been cured | A doctor's bag | A germ that cannot spread | *A changed form of the germ
test: «Ben solved a variant of the maths problem with bigger numbers.» What does variant mean in this sentence? | A problem nobody can solve | A wrong answer | A problem with no numbers | *A slightly different version of the problem
exam: The list showed a variant spelling of the word. What does variant mean here? | *A different but accepted way to spell it | A spelling mistake to be deleted | A list with no letters | A word that is not in the dictionary
